# What deploy-lan-web.sh does not sync, and the ONLY thing the drift check is
# allowed to be blind to. One file, two readers, so the guard and the rsync it
# guards cannot drift apart.
#
# rsync --delete does not delete what it excludes, so this list is also the
# protection list: a path in here survives a deploy, and a path not in here is
# either replaced from the repo or DELETED. That is why the drift check reads
# this file rather than keeping its own idea of what to look at.
#
# Format is rsync's, restricted to two shapes the Python side also implements:
#   name/    a directory of that name, at any depth (glob allowed)
#   glob     a file whose basename matches, at any depth
# Anything else -- a pattern with a slash in the middle, an anchored /path --
# makes ktp-lan-web-drift.py exit 2 rather than guess.

# Python bytecode, regenerated on import.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The venv is built on the box and is not ours to manage.
venv/
.venv/
node_modules/

.git/

# Hand-deploy fossils from before this script existed. They sit above app/, so
# this is belt and braces -- but if one ever lands inside app/, it is preserved
# rather than deleted.
.deploy-bak-*/
